From 92a64fccdbba415a536da084ed09d74909d620d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim auf der Landwehr <tadl-git@taufderl.de>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:53:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: qdsp6: add the voice services; wire them up on
 the FP4

Call audio on this SoC needs the QDSP6 voice services (MVM/CVS/CVP) and a
voice PCM for a userspace daemon (q6voiced) to hold during a call.
sm6350-mainline has none of it.

- The drivers (q6voice, q6voice-common, q6voice-dai, q6mvm, q6cvs, q6cvp
  and dt-bindings/sound/qcom,q6voice.h), ported from sdm670-mainline with
  the LPI_MI2S AFE family stripped (SM7225's q6afe has no widgets for it,
  and a route to a missing widget fails the whole card) and CODEC_DMA
  RX_0 / TX_3 wired into the voice mixers (where SM7225 has its codec).
- TX vocproc topology defaults to TOPOLOGY_ID_NONE: the SM_ECNS default
  needs ACDB calibration this device does not have and gives a silent
  uplink. sc7280-mainline made the same choice for the Fairphone 5.
- sm6350.dtsi: q6mvm (with the q6voice-dais child), q6cvs, q6cvp APR
  services.
- sm7225-fairphone-fp4: CS-VOICE and VoiceMMode1 front-end links.

Proven by a call on 2026-09-23 on a hand-built 7.2.0 kernel; this is the
same code rebased onto sm6350-7.2.y.
